    15	(GeoJSON pages of a WFS GetFeature; the stored hit count must equal the features read),
    16	`rules.yaml` holds per-input field rules, and `osd verify --outline-inputs` in the verify
    17	workflow compares committed outlines with today's inputs. Sixteen records point their
    18	`manifest_url` at an ArcGIS Map or Feature Server layer (`src/osd/verifier/samples.yaml`
    19	comments "ArcGIS layer"): nzpam/petroleum-wells (1,302 features), nzpam/seismic-surveys-2d (990),
    20	wa-demirs/petroleum-wells (4,371), sgudds/register-geotermalnych-vrtov (307), va-energy/gas-oil-wells
    21	(8,605), nd-dmr/wells (44,018), sk-mer/vertical-wells (119,595), sk-mer/drill-core (104,754),
    22	pgi/cbdg-boreholes (334,145), cgs/vrtna-prozkoumanost (746,789), bcer/well-surface-holes-permitted,
    23	sgc/banco-informacion-petrolera-pozos, ut-dogm/oil-gas-wells, and others listed there. ArcGIS
    24	layers page with `resultOffset`/`resultRecordCount` up to `maxRecordCount` per page and answer
    25	`f=geojson` where the server supports it; `supportsPagination` and `maxRecordCount` are in the
    26	layer's `?f=json` description. The verify run on main takes about 40 minutes today under a
    27	60-minute job timeout.
    28	
    29	**The design the lane must map to.**
    30	1. `format: arcgis` in `src/osd/outlines/`: read the layer description, page the whole layer with
    31	   `resultOffset`, in `f=geojson` when supported else `f=json` converted, `outSR=4326`; the stored
    32	   feature count must equal the layer's `returnCountOnly=true` count on the day (the WFS hit-count
    33	   rule), else the input is refused and the record keeps its level. Geometry types: point, line,
    34	   polygon, as the layer states. Dates from the fields `rules.yaml` names for the input (E18
    35	   `period_fields`), epoch milliseconds converted to ISO dates, UTC.
    36	2. Budget: one input is read in full or not at all; a layer above 50,000 features is out of scope
    37	   this lane (sk-mer, pgi, cgs stay at their level; the PR names them and the count on the day).
    38	   The verify job's total time with the new inputs stays under 60 minutes; the strategy says how
    39	   it is measured (the branch run's duration) and the lane stops adding inputs when the run
    40	   passes 50 minutes.
    41	3. Records (exact edits): `inputs` added to nzpam/petroleum-wells, nzpam/seismic-surveys-2d,
    42	   wa-demirs/petroleum-wells, sgudds/register-geotermalnych-vrtov, va-energy/gas-oil-wells,
    43	   nd-dmr/wells, bcer/well-surface-holes-permitted, sgc/banco-informacion-petrolera-pozos,
    44	   ut-dogm/oil-gas-wells, and any other ArcGIS-listed record under 50,000 features, each with
    45	   `name`, `url` (the layer, not a query), `format: arcgis`, `crs` and `stated` as the publisher
    46	   states it; rules in `rules.yaml`. No other field of those records changes.
    47	4. STAC: one Item per feature as E18 does for WFS inputs, `osd:period_source: feature` where the
    48	   layer states dates; the full-tree validation step (OSD-D18) stays green.
    49	5. Site: nothing new; tiles (E15) carry the points. A phone-width screenshot of one new register
    50	   zoomed in is evidence, not a change.
    51	
    52	**Acceptance.**
    53	- Fixture ArcGIS server (injected responses, offline): paged reads reassemble the layer exactly;
    54	  a count mismatch refuses the input; a page error refuses the input; `f=json` fallback converts
    55	  geometry correctly for point, polyline and polygon; dates from epoch ms are exact. One mutation
    56	  per guard (count check removed, pagination stop condition broken, date conversion off by a day).
    57	- `osd verify --outline-inputs` for the new records on the branch run: each either L3 with the
    58	  feature count, or refused with the reason printed.
    59	- The branch verify run completes under 60 minutes; the PR states its duration.
    60	- The STAC tree validates (full step) with the new Items; the PR gives the Item count per record.
    61	- The record diffs show only `inputs`.
    62	
    63	**Out of scope.** Layers above 50,000 features; WFS or other formats; verifier listing changes
    64	(E23's ArcGIS export reader stays as it is); any site code.
    65	
    66	**Stop rules.** If the verify job cannot stay under 60 minutes with any new input, stop after
    67	the fixture work and write the finding (split verify into a matrix, or cache inputs) for a
    68	hardening charter.
    69	
    70	**Ownership and dependencies.** Coding lane; paths `src/osd/outlines/**`, `src/osd/verify.py`
    71	(outline input dispatch only, if needed), `tests/test_outlines.py` additions, `tests/fixtures/outlines/**`,
    72	`outlines/**` for the new records, the records named in design 3 (`inputs` only), `schema/outline.schema.json`
    73	only if a bump is unavoidable (name it in the PR title), `docs/program/evidence/e29/**`. Depends
    74	on E03, E18, E23, E25 (merged). E28 (periods) must not edit the design-3 records.
    75	
    76	**Evidence to inspect.** The fixture tests and mutations; the branch run's verify output and
    77	duration; the record diffs; one screenshot.
